  "body": "## What changed\nThe test `a_kind_that_is_not_a_kind_refuses_at_the_door` in `crates/app/tests/machine.rs` now uses \"drill press\" as the illegal kind word. It used \"router\" before. Three lines change (605, 607, 614). No product code changes.\n\n## Cause\nPR #3279 made \"router\" a legal kind word (`crates/post/src/machine/kind.rs`, `Kind::from_word`). The word now reads as a mill. `parse_mch` no longer refuses it, so the `expect_err` in the test panics. The post-merge gate on main failed for this reason (run 45007275047). \"drill press\" is not a kind and not an alias.\n\n## Readings\n- `cargo xtask gate test a_kind_that_is_not_a_kind_refuses_at_the_door --crate camcraft-app --binary machine --exact`: `test a_kind_that_is_not_a_kind_refuses_at_the_door ... ok`, `test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 32 filtered out`.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test machine` (whole binary): `test result: ok. 33 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out`.\n\nBoth runs used exactly the content of the head commit.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The quick gate did not complete. The local `main` ref of the main checkout is behind `origin/main`, so the gate chose the batch plan (1150 changed files). The run stopped because of disk space. The diff touches only `crates/app/tests/machine.rs`, and its one test binary ran in full.\n- Clippy did not run.\n- Heavy lanes did not run. The diff reaches none of them.\n\nEffort: low\nProcess change: no\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3337\n",
